			TEXT("\n    Lambert diffuse BRDF - simplest physically-based diffuse model.\n    Assumes perfectly diffuse (Lambertian) surface with uniform scattering.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    - albedo: Surface color (diffuse reflectance)\n    - n_dot_l: Dot product of normal and light direction (pre-clamped to [0,1])\n    \n    Returns: Diffuse contribution (albedo / π * n_dot_l)\n    \n    Usage:\n        let n_dot_l = max(dot(normal, light_dir), 0.0)\n        let diffuse = lambert_diffuse(material.albedo, n_dot_l)\n    \n    Reference: Lambert's cosine law (1760)\n    ");
