			TEXT("\n    Complete PBR direct lighting calculation for a single light source.\n    Combines diffuse (Lambert) and specular (Cook-Torrance) terms with energy conservation.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    - albedo: Surface base color\n    - metallic: Metallic factor [0.0 = dielectric, 1.0 = metal]\n    - roughness: Surface roughness [0.0 = smooth, 1.0 = rough]\n    - normal: Surface normal (normalized)\n    - view_dir: Direction to camera (normalized)\n    - light_dir: Direction to light (normalized)\n    - light_color: Light color (linear RGB)\n    - light_intensity: Light intensity multiplier\n    \n    Returns: Outgoing radiance for this light\n    \n    Usage:\n        let radiance = pbr_direct_lighting(\n            material.albedo,\n            material.metallic,\n            material.roughness,\n            normal,\n            view_dir,\n            light_dir,\n            light.color,\n            light.intensity\n        )\n    \n    Reference: Cook-Torrance BRDF (1982), PBR theory\n    ");
			TEXT("");
