			TEXT("\n    Henyey-Greenstein phase function for anisotropic scattering.\n    Models how light scatters in participating media (clouds, fog, smoke).\n    \n    Parameters:\n    - cos_theta: Cosine of angle between light direction and view direction\n    - g: Anisotropy factor [-1.0 = back-scatter, 0.0 = isotropic, 1.0 = forward-scatter]\n    \n    Returns: Phase function value (probability of scattering in view direction)\n    \n    Usage:\n        let cos_theta = dot(light_dir, view_dir)\n        let phase = henyey_greenstein(cos_theta, 0.6)  # Forward scattering\n        let in_scatter = light_color * phase * density\n    \n    Reference: Henyey & Greenstein (1941)\n    ");
